Z||000012||StuGood||07-22-2001||08:06 PM||||Maybe it's a real idiot light - no bulb, just sits there with that blank look... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>How about this theory?  For right-hand drive Fieros, they wanted to swap speedo and tach gages (used a different flexcircuit on the IP), so they provided on odometer slot on both sides of the panel?  AusFiero might know.<P>Just a stab  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000013||Pontiaddict||07-22-2001||10:15 PM||||It's was the crank rotation counter, (can't remember the technical name) GM was going to pit it there as a joke to show how many times the crank turned before the 84 Dukes blew apart. That's why it's on the tach side.<BR>They pulled the counter at the last minute when they thought that the information could be used aginst them.<P>True Story<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="555555">Yeah right.</FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000014||Fiero_24||07-22-2001||10:46 PM||||My guess has always been for park, neutral, drive, drive2, drive 3.  The old monte carlo's had them there so you could see on the dash what you were shifting to.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||3
